    goals: "Start ART, prevent OIs, manage IRIS, screen for TB/Crypto, partner notification, prevent transmission",
    pharm: "1. Start ART: Tenofovir Disoproxil Fumarate 300mg daily + Lamivudine 300mg daily + Dolutegravir 50mg daily (TLD regimen — preferred first-line in Kenya). 2. OI Prophylaxis: Start CTX (Co-trimoxazole) 960mg daily (for CD4 <200, continues until CD4 >200 for 6 months). 3. TB Preventive Therapy (TPT): Isoniazid 300mg daily + Pyridoxine 25mg daily for 6 months (after ruling out active TB). 4. If CD4 <100: Cryptococcal antigen screening. 5. Screen for STIs and treat if positive. 6. Immunisations: PCV13, PPSV23, annual influenza. Assess for hepatitis B and treat if co-infected.",
