    goals: "Eradicate Salmonella Typhi, resolve fever, prevent complications (intestinal perforation, haemorrhage, chronic carriage)",
    pharm: "1. First-line empiric therapy: Oral Azithromycin 1g daily for 7 days (preferred due to increasing fluoroquinolone resistance). 2. Alternative: IV Ceftriaxone 2g daily for 10-14 days (if severe, vomiting, or complications). 3. If fluoroquinolone-susceptible confirmed: Ciprofloxacin 500mg BID for 10 days (check sensitivity first). 4. Do NOT use Amoxicillin or Co-trimoxazole (high resistance). 5. Antipyretics: Paracetamol 1g QID PRN. 6. Avoid anti-motility agents for diarrhoea.",
